   "date": "2018-05-29T22:44:57Z",
   "subject": "Define new variable that is not a combination of others",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear all,</div><div><br></div><div></div><div>in Mplus, you often see code like this:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">MODEL CONSTRAINT</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    NEW </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rho</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span></div></code></div><div><br>Is there a way to define variables in such a way in lavaan, that is, by only providing the starting value of the new variable?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance!</div><div><br></div><div>Marcus<br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ALwlCsVJAAAJ",
   "from": "Yves Rosseel",
   "author": "89c9fc822e34b78c",
   "date": "2018-05-31T16:23:45Z",
   "subject": "Re: Define new variable that is not a combination of others",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On 05/30/2018 12:44 AM, &#39;Marcus&#39; via lavaan wrote:\r<br>&gt; Dear all,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; in Mplus, you often see code like this:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt; MODEL CONSTRAINT:\r<br>&gt;      NEW (rho*.8beta*0);\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Is there a way to define variables in such a way in lavaan, that is, by \r<br>&gt; only providing the starting value of the new variable?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Do you mean you wish to &#39;fix&#39; the new variable to a starting value (and \r<br>not use it any further?).\r<br>\r<br>You can write this:\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>HS.model &lt;- &#39; visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3\r<br>               textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6\r<br>               speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9\r<br>\r<br>               newpar := 4\r<br>&#39;\r<br>\r<br>But perhaps you have something else in mind?\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
